# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenLock Android
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Gradle / build output -------------------------------------------------
.gradle/
build/
captures/
.cxx/
.externalNativeBuild/
local.properties
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
*.class
output.json
output-metadata.json

# Scoped to the repository root on purpose. A bare `release/` also matches
# app/src/release/, which is a standard Android source set - a file placed
# there would be ignored with no warning at all. Build output already lives
# under `build/`.
/release/

# --- IDE -------------------------------------------------------------------
*.iml
.idea/
.kotlin/
.kotlin-cache/
*.hprof
*.log

# --- Signing ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Passwords never go in the repository.
keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# The one deliberate exception: the release keystore is committed so CI can
# sign every build with the same identity. Without it each GitHub runner
# generates a fresh debug key, and no two builds can upgrade-install over each
# other. The passwords stay in GitHub Secrets - the key file alone is useless
# without them.
#
# NOTE: keep every comment on its own line. A trailing comment becomes part of
# the pattern and the rule silently stops matching. The negation must also come
# after the `*.jks` rule above, and `keystore/` must not itself be excluded.
!keystore/openlock-release.jks

# --- OS ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
